<title>USA: U.S. cattle group welcomes veterinary drug bill.</title>
<headline>U.S. cattle group welcomes veterinary drug bill.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. National Cattlemen's Beef Association welcomed Thursday passage of a new bill to streamline approval for veterinary medicines.</p>
<p>Connie Greig, chairperson of NCBA's animal health committee, said the bill -- approved Wednesday -- will mean a clearer procedure for clearance for veterinary medicines by the Food and Drug Administration.</p>
<p>&quot;Unnecessary delays in approval of new products have deprived the livestock industry and consumers of increased efficiency in production,&quot; Grieg said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
</text>
